# Scholars Who Work With Technology Fear They Suffer in Tenure Reviews.

**Authors:** Guernsey, Lisa

## Abstract
College faculty, particularly in the humanities, are finding institutions do not always treat substantial work with electronic media as a form of scholarship or service. While more humanities departments are embracing technology, faculty are finding involvement in innovative projects risky to their careers. Professional associations are criticized for not addressing the issue adequately. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ547630

